tweets.text:
Secretary Noem’s visit to Bahrain made history as the first US Homeland Security Secretary to visit the @USCG Patrol Forces Southwest Asia. Bahrain houses one of America’s largest and most strategic bases in the region with six USCG Cutters and 200+ personnel providing security for our Navy and shipping industry. 

@Sec_Noem met with Coast Guard personnel to reiterate @POTUS Trump’s desire to rebuild the Coast Guard into the world’s finest maritime fighting force through Force Design 2028.

While there, Secretary Noem met with King Hamad bin Isa Al Khalifa to reaffirm the countries’ 50+ year friendship and discuss US security assets in Bahrain.

